            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0684" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./241:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-07T13:00:00-05:00">February 7, 1929—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Your 15, February 6, 11 a.m. On account of delay in receiving permit for
                    survey flight to Colombia, Pan American Airways had arranged for Lindbergh to
                    remain in Panama until return flight to this country, which must start at 6 a.m.
                    Sunday. If permission is received for the survey flight in time for Lindbergh to
                    make flight to Barranquilla and return tomorrow, an effort will be made to have
                    him do this. It is doubtful whether Lindbergh would be able to make the flight
                    Saturday, in view of the necessity for starting return flight Sunday.</p>
                <p>Please convey the situation tactfully to the appropriate authorities and
                    communicate any further developments direct to Legation at Panama as well as to
                    the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
